  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nBrowsers fire the `change` event on textarea elements, like input and select do.\nhttps://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?%3C!DOCTYPE%20html%3E%0A%3Ctextarea%20onchange%3D%22this.style.backgroundColor%3D'honeydew'%3B%20w('change')%22%3EEdit%20text%20here%20and%20blur%3C%2Ftextarea%3E\n\nI couldn't find where the current spec explicitly defines firing `change` for textarea. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#event-change lists \"Form controls\" as the target for `change`. So I think the intent is that textarea should support it.\n\nHowever, https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-textarea-element only mentions the `input` event. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#unfocus-causes-change-event also says it only checks \"If _entry_ is an `input` element\".\n\nOr am I missing something?",
